2191372, "avatar": "fef49e7fa7e1997310d705b2a6158ff8dc1cdfeb"}, "language": "english", "review": "SPACE NINJAS", "timestamp_created": 1699396043, "timestamp_updated": 1699396043, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1364234640", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "149728240", "author": {"steamid": "76561198087385380", "personaname": "lune 花", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/pepperlune/", "num_games_owned": 135, "num_reviews": 3, "playtime_forever": 281789, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 89, "playtime_at_review": 236730, "last_played": 1789428854, "avatar": "96c2efefa8616fabfe58b6e09d5baf3624dad3d7"}, "language": "english", "review": "Mind-numbing, soul-crushing, and excruciating - these are the emotions that wash over me every time I dive into this game these days. With each new patch or update, I secretly hope that maybe, just maybe, things will improve, only to be met with disappointment yet again.\n\nI find myself pondering when and how it all took a nosedive. It's akin to watching a tree being slowly felled by a diligent lumberjack who makes a daily incision. In the case of this game, there's no glaring, monumental flaw to pinpoint. Instead, it's an unending stream of minor missteps that relentlessly gnaw at my sanity.\n\nThe illusion of scale often blinds us. The average player revels in the staggering array of activities, the endless loot to amass, and the countless trinkets to decorate their proverbial trophy shelf. However, it was only after the thousandth expedition into the mines that I realized I wasn't collecting diamonds but rather meaningless ore. These ores vary in size and shape, but they all amount to nothing.\n\nAs for the story, it leaves much to be desired. Ballas started as a captivating villain, especially from the moment we first heard his voice in The Second Dream. The revelation about Umbra and the methods of his creation left us in shock. We believed Ballas to be the ultimate threat. \n\nYet, the instant I witnessed this cunning blue devil being dragged in chains and treated like a pet by Erra, I couldn't help but think, \"It's all over.\" No words can capture the disappointment of seeing an antagonist I had such high hopes for reduced to this pitiful state by an enemy we had only recently encountered.\n\nSave yourself from the misery I've endured. I've gone too far down this rabbit hole. If I could turn back time and recoup the hours I've lost, I'd do it without hesitation. Regret is my constant companion.\n\nBeware, all you who are enticed by the game's charms, for it's a trap. You'll only realize you're ensnared when it's too late to break free.", "timestamp_created": 1699394779, "timestamp_updated": 1699394779, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 22, "votes_funny": 1, "weighted_vote_score": "0.589790582656860352", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1364234640", "reactions": [{"reaction_type": 6, "count": 3}, {"reaction_type": 5, "count": 2}, {"reaction_type": 16, "count": 1}, {"reaction_type": 8, "count": 1}]}]}